course: dictionary
lesson: 10463
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the words around the word tell you which meaning the writer means. This is context again: the clues are in the sentence.
explain: «Kwesi's mum sends Tom home with a tub of her jollof rice.» The words «of her jollof rice» tell you what is inside the tub, so a tub here is a container for food.
explain: «Clothes were boiled in a big tub called a copper.» This tub is a large container for washing, not for food. Ask yourself: what is it holding? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some tubs are baths. In American English, a tub is the bath you wash in, so «a hot tub» can mean a bath. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A tub is a wide, open container, often round, for holding food, plants or water.
fact: «A tub of ice cream» means a container full of ice cream.
fact: In American English, a tub can mean a bathtub, the bath you wash in.
fact: A tub can also be a small plastic box with a lid, for food like yoghurt or margarine.
fact: «Washtub» means a tub used for washing clothes.
exercise: «Tom goes home with a tub of jollof rice.» In this sentence, what is a tub? | A railway carriage | *A container holding food | A bath to wash in | A type of rice
exercise: «Clothes were boiled in a big tub called a copper.» What were the clothes boiled in? | A bath for washing yourself | *A large tub used for washing clothes | A bowl for soup | A small plastic box with a lid
exercise: The word tub has more than one meaning. What helps you choose the right one? | How many letters it has | Whether it has a capital letter | *The words around it in the sentence | Always picking the first meaning in the list
test: «He says he loves washing and is never so happy as with both arms in the wash-tub.» What is a wash-tub? | *A large container for washing | A cupboard for towels | A kind of soap
test: Which word is the best swap for tub in «a tub of ice cream»? | Cloud | *Container | Ruler
exam: In which sentence does tub mean a bath? | The tub of soup was hot. | *She sat in the hot tub and relaxed. | She put the tub of cream in the fridge.
